<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 3 October, from 42 BCE to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/42-bce">42 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,067 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Antony and Octavian fight Brutus and Cassius at Philippi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the first battle of Philippi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> defeated Cassius and took his camp, while Brutus overran Octavian's troops. The battle was a tactical draw, but Cassius, believing it lost, took his own life to avoid capture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-philippi">Battle of Philippi</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-cassius-longinus">Gaius Cassius Longinus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">382 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,644 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodosius I settles the Goths inside the Roman Empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> concluded a treaty allowing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> to settle south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> as semi-autonomous allies. Giving a whole people land within the frontier set a precedent that reshaped the late Roman world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">610 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,416 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Heraclius the Younger's rebel fleet reaches Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The fleet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> the Younger, who with his father, the Exarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, had rebelled against Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocas">Phocas</a> in 608, reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. Heraclius went on to execute Phocas and be proclaimed emperor, founding the Heraclian dynasty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/assisi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assisi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1226">1226 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">800 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francis of Assisi dies at the Porziuncola</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Francis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assisi">Assisi</a> died at the Porziuncola chapel below Assisi. The merchant's son who embraced radical poverty had founded the Franciscan order, and he was canonised less than two years later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1283">1283 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">743 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dafydd ap Gruffydd, last native Prince of Wales, is executed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dafydd-ap-gruffydd">Dafydd ap Gruffydd</a>, who had claimed the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> after his brother Llywelyn's death, was hanged, drawn and quartered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrewsbury">Shrewsbury</a> on the orders of Edward I. He was the last native Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> before Edward's conquest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dafydd-ap-gruffydd">Dafydd ap Gruffydd</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln proclaims a national day of Thanksgiving</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Amid the Civil War, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> proclaimed the last Thursday of November a national day of thanksgiving. The proclamation answered years of campaigning by the editor Sarah Josepha Hale and began an annual federal holiday.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1929">1929 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Alexander renames his realm the Kingdom of Yugoslavia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> renamed the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, 'land of the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>', as part of his royal dictatorship. The new name was meant to override the national rivalries dividing the state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1990">1990 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany is reunified</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">German Democratic Republic</a> acceded to the Federal Republic, reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> 45 years after its division. The peaceful merger, less than a year after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a> opened, marked the close of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 3 October <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-ross-cherokee-chief"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-ross-cherokee-chief.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Ross (Cherokee chief)</span><span class="tp">1790–1866</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-grand-duke-of-tuscany"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-ii-grand-duke-of-tuscany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leopold II, Grand Duke of Tuscany</span><span class="tp">1797–1870</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nicolas-avellaneda"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nicolas-avellaneda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nicolás Avellaneda</span><span class="tp">1837–1885</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 3 October <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-zayd"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Muhammad ibn Zayd</span><span class="tp">d. 900</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/iziaslav-i-of-kiev"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/iziaslav-i-of-kiev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Iziaslav I of Kiev</span><span class="tp">1024–1078</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dafydd-ap-gruffydd"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Dafydd ap Gruffydd</span><span class="tp">c. 1238–1283</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-maultasch"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margaret-maultasch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margaret Maultasch</span><span class="tp">1318–1369</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-barclay"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Robert Barclay</span><span class="tp">1648–1690</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gustav-stresemann"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gustav-stresemann.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gustav Stresemann</span><span class="tp">1878–1929</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
